<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Where's the Puddle? – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> It's the Rainy Season</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Where's the Puddle?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: productive: Narrate a short story or incident that is happening now. interactive: Engage in simple exchanges about personal interests.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can narrate, using basic descriptive phrases, a simple current event related to rainy weather (e.g., 'It is raining today, and I am jumping in puddles.'). Can engage in simple exchanges about activities during rainy weather with peers (e.g., 'What do you like to do when it rains?' 'I like to read inside.'). Can collaborate with classmates to give a short presentation on rainy day activities they like to do (e.g., 'We bring umbrellas and boots when it rains.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows a large picture of children playing in puddles during a rainy day. The teacher asks, "What do you see?" and elicits words like 'rain,' 'puddle,' 'boots,' 'umbrella.' The teacher then asks, "What is the weather like?" encouraging 'It is rainy' or 'It is pouring.'</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher points to a child in the picture and says, "Look! It is raining. He is wearing boots. He is jumping in a puddle. He likes to splash!" The teacher models the pronunciation of /r/ in 'rain' and /p/ in 'puddle' clearly, asking students to repeat individually and chorally. "Repeat after me: *rain*, *puddle*, *splash*."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is the boy sleeping in the puddle?" (No, he is jumping.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is it sunny in the picture?" (No, it is rainy.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[5-7 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "It's the Rainy Season".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, illustrated dialogue between two children, Leo and Mia, discussing their rainy day activities. The dialogue will be displayed on a projector or large flashcards, clearly depicting actions and items.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example Dialogue Excerpt:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Mia:</b> "Oh no, look! It is pouring rain today."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Leo:</b> "Yes, the sky is gloomy. But I like rainy days! I am wearing my new raincoat and boots. I am going puddle-jumping!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Mia:</b> "That's fun! I need my umbrella. What do you do when it rains, Leo?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Leo:</b> "I like to splash! Where is the biggest puddle?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Narrating current events related to weather (using Present Continuous). Talking about rainy weather and sharing experiences (using Present Simple and WH-questions).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher reads the dialogue aloud, pointing to the speakers. Students listen and follow along.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What are Leo and Mia talking about?" (Rainy days / What they do in the rain.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "Leo is wearing sandals." (False) "Mia needs an umbrella." (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match pictures of items (umbrella, boots, raincoat) to the child who uses them.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[8-10 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Grammar: Present simple (What do you need?), Present continuous (It is raining today; I am jumping.), WH-questions (What do you wear?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Vocabulary: puddle, umbrella, raincoat, boots, splash, wet, rainy, muddy.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation: /r/ in 'rain' and /p/ in 'puddle.' Blending sounds for 'muddy' and 'sky.'</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pragmatic: Talking about rainy weather; Sharing experiences.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion Chain:</b> The teacher starts a sentence orally, and students take turns completing it, focusing on target vocabulary and grammar. Each student builds on the previous one.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "It is raining today, so I need a..."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student 1: "...raincoat."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student 2: "When it is rainy, I wear my..."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student 3: "...boots."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "I see a big..."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student 4: "...puddle. I want to splash!"</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Picture Description with Prompts (Pair Work):</b> The teacher displays various pictures of children doing activities in the rain (e.g., a child with an umbrella, a child puddle-jumping, someone looking at a gloomy sky). In pairs, students describe the pictures using given sentence frames.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "Look at this picture. It is ______ (rainy/gloomy). What is the boy/girl doing?"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B: "He/She is ______ (jumping/splashing/walking) in a puddle. He/She is wearing ______ (boots/raincoat). The puddle is ______ (wet/muddy)."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students swap roles for different pictures, practicing phonemic awareness by spelling 'muddy' and 'sky' if applicable.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - "Ask Your Partner":</b> Students work in pairs to ask and answer WH-questions about their preferences and actions during rainy weather.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What do you like to do when it rains?" (I like to read inside. / I like to play board games.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What do you wear when it is rainy?" (I wear my raincoat and boots.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do you like to puddle-jump?" (Yes, I do! / No, I don't.)</li>
                        </ul>
                        The teacher circulates, providing feedback on pronunciation and grammar, especially /r/ and /p/ sounds.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[15-18 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "It's the Rainy Season".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative "Rainy Day Storytelling Chain" and short group presentation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work in small groups of 3-4.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher starts a simple story related to the theme "Where's the Puddle?" and the scenario "It's the Rainy Season." For example: "It is raining today, and I see a big, muddy puddle on the street."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each student in the group takes turns adding one sentence to the story, continuing the narrative. They must use the present continuous tense (e.g., "He is running," "She is splashing") and target vocabulary. They are encouraged to use WH-questions to prompt each other if they get stuck (e.g., "What is he wearing?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher encourages fluency and natural interaction, focusing on communication rather than perfect accuracy at this stage.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After 3-4 minutes, each group presents their short, collaborative story to the class. The group collaboratively gives a short presentation on rainy day activities they like to do. For example, "We bring umbrellas and boots when it rains. We like to splash."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example Story Progression:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher: "It is raining today, and I see a big, muddy puddle on the street."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student 1: "A boy is running to the puddle. He is wearing a yellow raincoat."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student 2: "He is wearing big, red boots. He wants to splash!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student 3: "Now he is jumping! He is splashing the water everywhere!"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[10-12 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the group presentations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their collaborative "Rainy Day Storytelling Chain" to the class, collectively narrating their short story.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (especially /r/ and /p/ sounds).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of at least 3 target vocabulary words (e.g., puddle, umbrella, boots, splash, muddy, raincoat).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Present Simple and Present Continuous (e.g., 'It is raining. He is jumping.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of message (narrating a simple current event related to rainy weather).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration with classmates during the storytelling and presentation.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick self-assessment before leaving.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">I can talk about rainy weather using words like 'puddle' and 'raincoat'. (Yes / A little / No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">I can tell what someone is doing in the rain using sentences like 'He is jumping'. (Yes / A little / No)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[5 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What new words can you use now to talk about the rain?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was your favorite rainy day activity to talk about with your classmates today?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this speaking lesson? Did students actively use the Present Continuous for current events and share experiences effectively?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for students who were less engaged in speaking activities? (e.g., more visual prompts, sentence starters).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How can I continue to reinforce the pronunciation of /r/ and /p/ sounds?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "Great job speaking about rainy days! Tomorrow, in Lesson 4, we will use the words and sentences we practiced today to write our own short stories about rainy day activities, focusing on writing composition."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[2-3 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>